# o1js proves with a shared WebAssembly.Memory, which is a SharedArrayBuffer,
# which the browser only hands to a cross-origin-isolated page. Without both of
# these headers the deposit flow fails at compile time, not at deploy time —
# they are load-bearing, not hardening.
#
# The dev server sets the same pair from next.config.mjs (ISOLATION_HEADERS),
# since headers() is dropped under output: "export". Change both together.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# The o1js compilation cache. A stale entry is harmless — o1js compares the
# header against the circuit's uniqueId and recompiles on a mismatch — so this
# can be cached hard.
/cache/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
